  "releaseNotes": "v5.2.2 - FIX: the OPFS model cache could not download from a WORKER. ModelCache.DownloadWithProgressAsync fetched via `window`, which does not exist in a WorkerGlobalScope, so it threw a bare NullReferenceException - and a worker is exactly where a model should be loaded. It now fetches from the runtime's global scope, which works in window, dedicated worker, shared worker and service worker alike. See Changelog.",
